<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hamilcar Barca</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 275–228 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hamilcar Barca was a Carthaginian general who commanded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> in the last years of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-punic-war">First Punic War</a> and then crushed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary-war">Mercenary War</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. In 237 BCE he led an army to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>, where he conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadalquivir">Guadalquivir</a> valley and its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> mines and founded a Carthaginian domain. He drowned in 228 BCE; his son-in-law Hasdrubal and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a> continued his work.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hamilcar-barca.jpg" alt="Hamilcar Barca" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Max Karl Baldamus · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amilcare_Barca_(Ritratto).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
